    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105-a3">

                <pb facs="0260" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg160"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    582.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ferry to Mr. Morton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-07-04"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 4,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Morton</hi>: As you may be aware, I have
                    been seriously indisposed, and in order properly to fulfil all my duties I have
                    to take certain precautions to which I am little accustomed.</p>
                <p>The work of yesterday was very fatiguing for me, and I have, therefore, been
                    ordered complete rest to-day.</p>
                <p>The Government of the Republic will be represented upon the occasion by several
                    ministers. Above all others, I shall feel regret at my inability to personally
                    attend this fete of the fraternity of the two great Republics; but you know that
                    I shall be there in the spirit, in heart, and in soul.</p>
                <p>Believe, my dear Mr. Morton, in my entire devotion.</p>
                <closer><signed>JULES FERRY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
